+Malformed double-negation, duplicate/conflicting option groups and unsupported regex-engine complexity are rejected as unsupported rules. Anchored IDN URL patterns use canonical hostnames. URL inputs above 65,536 characters fail open with an explicit input-limit reason and are not retained in the origin history. A single regex can still run up to its timeout beyond the cooperative scan deadline. See [security limitations](SECURITY-LIMITATIONS.md) and [test matrix](TEST-MATRIX.md).
+
+Local UTF-8 import now enforces the 8 MB bound while reading, supports a UTF-8 BOM, rejects invalid bytes and displays the content SHA-256 before Apply. Reading runs off the UI thread. The digest identifies bytes; without a trusted expected digest/signature it does not authenticate a publisher. No network updater or automatic replacement is enabled.
